## Why This Is Asked
This question tests cross-account data governance, privacy controls, and practical automation in AWS, focusing on how to protect tenant data during ingestion.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account data ingestion and event routing via EventBridge
- Per-tenant IAM roles with least-privilege access
- Per-tenant KMS keys for encryption isolation
- Centralized Lambda for PII redaction with tenant-specific rules
- Infrastructure-as-Code for safe onboarding and teardown
- Versioned redaction rules and raw data retention for rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda redaction layer
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const kms = new AWS.KMS();

const REDACTION_RULES = {
  default: {
    email: (v) => v ? 'REDACTED' : null,
    phone: (v) => v ? 'REDACTED' : null,
  },
  tenantA: {
    ssn: (v) => v ? '***-**-' + v.slice(-4) : null,
  }
};

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenantId = event.detail.tenantId;
  const rules = REDACTION_RULES[tenantId] || REDACTION_RULES.default;

  const redacted = { ...event.detail };
  for (const [field, redactionFn] of Object.entries(rules)) {
    if (redacted[field]) {
      redacted[field] = redactionFn(redacted[field]);
    }
  }

  await s3.putObject({
    Bucket: process.env.DATA_LAKE_BUCKET,
    Key: `${tenantId}/${Date.now()}/${event.id}.json`,
    Body: JSON.stringify(redacted)
  }).promise();

  return { statusCode: 200 };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical, beginner-friendly multi-tenant quota control using AWS SaaS patterns. It tests understanding of API Gateway usage plans, Lambda authorizers, DynamoDB for counters, and EventBridge for automated overage handling, plus testing strategies.

## Key Concepts
- API Gateway usage plans and API keys for tenant isolation
- Lambda authorizers and IAM policy generation
- DynamoDB design: tenantId partition key, windowed counters with TTL
- Exponential backoff, throttling, and automated suspensions
- Basic test strategies: unit, integration, and end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton of a Lambda authorizer that enforces per-tenant quotas
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { apiKey } = event.requestContext.identity;
  const tenantId = await getTenantIdFromApiKey(apiKey);

  // Check remaining quota in DynamoDB
  const quota = await checkQuota(tenantId);

  if (quota.remaining <= 0) {
    return generateDenyPolicy(tenantId);
  }

  // Decrement counter and allow access
  await decrementQuota(tenantId);
  return generateAllowPolicy(tenantId);
};
```

